WEBVTT

00:11.062 --> 00:14.083
Rimuru-sensei,
you're the king of this nation?!

00:14.083 --> 00:17.083
Ms. Tiss was so shocked,
she passed out!

00:17.083 --> 00:19.059
She did?!

00:19.059 --> 00:21.075
Well, this is a problem.

00:21.075 --> 00:23.096
Without someone to supervise you, then...

00:23.096 --> 00:25.000
What's wrong?

01:33.007 --> 01:38.002
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

02:00.056 --> 02:03.077
EPISODE 68: THE FOUNDER'S FESTIVAL
Hey, Sensei! Who is she?

02:03.077 --> 02:07.067
This is Hinata. She's so strong,
we fought to a tie once.

02:08.015 --> 02:09.073
Whaaat?! A tie with this old...

02:11.003 --> 02:13.047
What were you about to say?

02:13.047 --> 02:15.032
U-Uh, I was going to say "pretty lady."

02:15.032 --> 02:17.062
K-Kei-chan!

02:17.062 --> 02:20.033
Don't be so rude, Kenya.

02:20.033 --> 02:22.083
She used to be Shizu-san's student, too.

02:23.079 --> 02:25.005
Are you talking about...

02:25.005 --> 02:29.017
The girl who got stronger than
Shizu-sensei in just a month...

02:29.017 --> 02:32.059
...Hinata Sakaguchi,
the captain of the Crusaders?!

02:32.059 --> 02:33.084
Wow!

02:33.084 --> 02:35.072
You should've told us that first.

02:35.072 --> 02:39.014
So, what were you concerned
about just now?

02:39.014 --> 02:44.085
Well, the person who was supposed
to watch over them couldn't go today.

02:44.085 --> 02:47.002
Fine, I'll babysit them.

02:47.002 --> 02:47.009
Huh?!

02:47.009 --> 02:50.065
What, are you trying to say
I'm not good enough for that?

02:50.065 --> 02:52.094
No, not at all.

02:52.094 --> 02:55.036
You kids won't say no
to me either, will you?

02:55.036 --> 02:57.003
No, of course not!

02:57.003 --> 02:59.003
- Ken-chan...
- Yes, by all means!

02:59.003 --> 03:00.066
You too, Gail?

03:00.066 --> 03:02.005
Then, all right.

03:02.005 --> 03:07.000
I can't believe I get to meet with
Hinata-oneesama! I look up to you so much!

03:07.000 --> 03:08.005
I like you!

03:09.000 --> 03:11.005
You remind me of Shizu-sensei!

03:14.072 --> 03:16.016
Well then, let's go.

03:16.016 --> 03:18.095
I heard they have yakisoba
and grilled corn.

03:18.095 --> 03:20.093
Let's start by checking out
the food stalls.

03:20.093 --> 03:21.051
Yes, ma'am!

03:22.089 --> 03:25.056
I will babysit the kids...

03:25.056 --> 03:27.094
But I'll have you take
care of Lady Luminus.

03:27.094 --> 03:29.069
Huh? Luminus?

03:29.069 --> 03:31.052
You invited her, didn't you?

03:32.004 --> 03:35.024
She gleefully prepared
a maid outfit for the occasion.

03:35.024 --> 03:36.003
Well then...

03:36.065 --> 03:38.007
I'm counting on you.

03:40.074 --> 03:44.029
Now I have much more
to worry about...

03:58.072 --> 04:00.089
That boy... It's Tact.

04:01.045 --> 04:05.014
He was depressed because he wasn't able to
be much help at the construction site...

04:07.056 --> 04:09.048
But look at him now.

04:47.031 --> 04:49.064
A harmony between humans and monsters.

04:50.023 --> 04:51.019
This is it.

04:51.073 --> 04:53.019
This is it!

05:02.095 --> 05:03.066
Shuna?

05:04.007 --> 05:04.091
Shion?!

05:05.037 --> 05:09.079
I knew they were doing something in secret,
but I didn't know it was for this.

05:09.079 --> 05:13.054
But Shuna aside,
can Shion actually perform?

06:24.053 --> 06:26.024
It was wonderful.

06:26.024 --> 06:27.091
Yes, wonderful indeed.

06:27.091 --> 06:30.004
I was so immersed
that I kept my eyes closed.

06:30.004 --> 06:31.058
Me too.

06:31.058 --> 06:33.054
I can still hear those
melodies in my ears.

06:33.054 --> 06:37.096
Man or monster,
what difference does it make?

06:37.096 --> 06:42.027
Indeed. What's good is good.
That's all there is to it.

06:43.003 --> 06:48.043
Music, arts, they connect
people across borders.

06:48.043 --> 06:52.068
There are things out there
that anyone can truly enjoy.

06:53.008 --> 06:55.019
That's what I like to believe in
at this moment.

06:55.062 --> 06:58.038
At least so I thought
from the bottom of my heart.

07:02.028 --> 07:03.082
What's this?! This is good!

07:03.082 --> 07:05.057
Yeah, good things are good.

07:06.007 --> 07:07.099
They transcend national boundaries.

07:10.074 --> 07:15.004
After the concert, we move on
to the science presentation for the afternoon.

07:17.000 --> 07:21.005
This a complete extraction from hipokute herbs
with all impurities removed.

07:21.005 --> 07:25.022
It boasts ninety-nine percent purity

07:25.022 --> 07:28.026
and possesses healing qualities
equivalent to a Full Potion.

07:28.026 --> 07:30.047
The audience looks bored.

07:30.047 --> 07:33.089
For the better or worse,
these two are too serious.

07:33.089 --> 07:38.048
Well, let's change our approach
and do a little scientific experiment.

07:39.081 --> 07:46.007
Now, can any of you answer whether
or not a potion can fix this sword?

07:46.007 --> 07:47.053
It's impossible!

07:47.053 --> 07:50.041
Hipokute herbs only work
on living things!

07:50.041 --> 07:55.058
Then how much does this rule apply?
What do you all think?

07:55.058 --> 07:56.091
Are you messing with us?!

07:56.091 --> 07:59.058
Effective scope of a healing potion, huh.

07:59.058 --> 08:01.067
That's certainly an interesting question.

08:01.067 --> 08:05.042
Is it whether it's alive or not?
No, that's not it...

08:05.088 --> 08:08.093
Just a guess, but maybe it's
the presence of a consciousness.

08:08.093 --> 08:09.008
Report.

08:09.008 --> 08:12.018
Consciousness has its roots in the soul.

08:12.018 --> 08:15.081
The presence or lack of a soul,
a collection of spiritual particles

08:15.081 --> 08:17.094
forming magicules,
is considered the difference.

08:17.094 --> 08:19.027
Right.

08:19.027 --> 08:22.077
Swords have no soul, therefore no will.

08:22.077 --> 08:24.044
They're just objects.

08:24.099 --> 08:26.036
No, hold on...

08:26.036 --> 08:29.078
Didn't Kaijin say that swords do have
a will of their own?

08:29.078 --> 08:30.074
Could it be...?!

08:30.074 --> 08:34.045
Heh-heh-heh. I would like
to know that as well.

08:34.045 --> 08:39.046
The desire to learn provides
the entryway to a new discovery!

08:39.046 --> 08:41.000
Indeed.

08:41.000 --> 08:45.021
I told him to stop such a ridiculous
experiment at first.

08:45.021 --> 08:48.003
But turned out I was the fool.

08:48.073 --> 08:53.085
I was so bound by common sense that I forgot
my original drives as a researcher.

08:56.039 --> 08:57.085
It stuck back!

08:57.085 --> 08:59.064
This is the answer.

08:59.064 --> 09:02.044
Although not recovered completely,

09:02.044 --> 09:06.023
the broken sword certainly
shows signs of repair.

09:06.023 --> 09:07.086
Unbelievable!

09:08.047 --> 09:11.074
Of course, you will only see
these effects on arms and armor

09:11.074 --> 09:16.056
that matured past a certain level,
and been used regularly by its owner.

09:17.062 --> 09:21.042
Why did you want to know
something like that?

09:22.017 --> 09:26.063
I found it hard to believe that plants
growing in the wild have their own wills.

09:26.063 --> 09:31.088
But after experimentation, we found
that healing potions work on them.

09:31.088 --> 09:35.087
That reminded me of
the existence of the dryads.

09:35.087 --> 09:38.014
They may have only a weak
consciousness at first,

09:38.014 --> 09:43.004
but over many months and years,
they can evolve into powerful monsters!

09:43.004 --> 09:45.052
The only things
that react to healing potion

09:45.052 --> 09:47.065
are those already
intertwined with magicules.

09:47.065 --> 09:52.007
Things with no magicules to them
at all show no reaction in our testing.

09:52.007 --> 09:56.003
Presented with these data,
a question arose in my mind.

09:56.003 --> 09:58.095
What is magicule?

09:58.095 --> 10:03.071
Here we have hipokute herbs
and grass you can find anywhere.

10:03.071 --> 10:07.046
We took an image of each structure
of the plant sample and enlarged them.

10:07.046 --> 10:10.034
Well then,
what do you think we found?

10:10.034 --> 10:11.067
What there is to find?

10:11.067 --> 10:17.022
A rare herb and an ordinary weed
already look as different as they can get.

10:17.022 --> 10:18.085
But can you believe this?

10:18.085 --> 10:21.077
The structures of hipokute herb
with its magicule extracted

10:21.077 --> 10:23.073
and ordinary weed are the same!

10:23.073 --> 10:27.086
That means, strictly speaking,
there's no such plant as hipokute herbs.

10:27.086 --> 10:31.094
They are actually mutated plants under
the influence of high-dense magicule!

10:31.094 --> 10:35.099
That's right! It's not that they grow
in magicule-rich areas,

10:35.099 --> 10:39.083
they're simple grass that mutates under
the influence of the high-dense magicule!

10:39.083 --> 10:43.058
That was the true identity
of the hipokute herbs!

10:45.021 --> 10:47.079
Th-This is a major discovery!

10:47.079 --> 10:53.009
S-Sir Vesta, this is not the type of thing
to announce in a place like this!

10:53.055 --> 10:58.076
There could've been a more appropriate occasion,
like in an academic conference!

10:58.076 --> 11:00.022
For real?

11:00.022 --> 11:03.048
Wait, now I think about it,
it all makes sense.

11:04.002 --> 11:06.069
It's hard to believe that
the cave Veldora was sealed in

11:06.069 --> 11:09.019
just so happens to be
full of hipokute herbs.

11:09.019 --> 11:12.004
If that was the result of a mutation,
then it checks out.

11:12.004 --> 11:17.041
Ores basked with magicule
turn into magicrystal, after all.

11:17.041 --> 11:21.087
I still don't have the answer
to my original question,

11:21.087 --> 11:24.075
of what is the exact nature of magicule.

11:24.075 --> 11:28.079
Despite this, we intend
to continue our research.

11:29.027 --> 11:31.057
We promise to keep pursuing
the answers in this land,

11:31.057 --> 11:34.001
where some of the world's
greatest minds are gathering...

11:34.001 --> 11:36.008
And with that,
we close our science presentation.

11:36.008 --> 11:38.034
Thank you very much...

11:38.034 --> 11:40.003
...for attending our presentation!

11:42.047 --> 11:47.002
With this, I'm sure there will be
a lot of researchers coming to Tempest.

11:47.002 --> 11:51.032
After all, in this magicule-rich land,
you can do research to your heart's content!

11:51.094 --> 11:54.053
You two did such a wonderful job!

11:56.007 --> 11:57.082
Thanks for your portage!

12:00.037 --> 12:02.002
Sensei!

12:02.066 --> 12:04.091
Oh, did you kids have fun?

12:04.091 --> 12:07.004
We ate so much, our tummies are full!

12:07.004 --> 12:10.008
We had hamburgers,
hotdog, and yakitori!

12:10.008 --> 12:12.017
They also have yakisoba!

12:12.017 --> 12:13.077
Sounds like all you do is eat.

12:13.077 --> 12:16.013
Isn't that a good thing?
Kids their age need to eat.

12:16.013 --> 12:20.009
You say that, but I'm sure you had
the most fun out of all of them.

12:20.009 --> 12:20.068
Huh?

12:25.031 --> 12:27.077
Whoa, wait, wait! Hold on!

12:28.048 --> 12:31.002
Arnaud and the others
were looking for you.

12:31.002 --> 12:33.044
They need to talk with you.

12:33.044 --> 12:34.022
Huh?

12:35.061 --> 12:38.007
I've brought him, Lady Luminus.

12:38.007 --> 12:43.045
Now, we have a nonaggression
treaty in place...

12:43.096 --> 12:45.002
But it's not enough.

12:45.002 --> 12:46.095
What's up so suddenly?

12:46.095 --> 12:48.058
What do you mean by that?

12:48.058 --> 12:50.071
What else can it be?

12:51.019 --> 12:52.092
I'm talking about exchanges!

12:52.092 --> 12:56.088
If we cannot make a deal with each other,
how will we ever have any exchanges?

12:56.088 --> 12:59.008
Uh, I don't see why we can't.

12:59.008 --> 13:02.055
You know, I heard Lubelius's
wheat is high quality,

13:02.055 --> 13:04.068
so I was hoping to import them someday.

13:04.068 --> 13:06.068
But the distance makes it difficult.

13:06.068 --> 13:08.081
How can you be so dense?

13:08.081 --> 13:11.052
When I say exchange,
I mean cultural exchange.

13:11.052 --> 13:14.036
Frankly, I underestimated all of you.

13:14.036 --> 13:17.036
That earlier performance was impressive.

13:17.036 --> 13:20.007
I have a newfound view of you today.

13:20.007 --> 13:24.012
There are some who are artistically
inclined among the vampires.

13:24.012 --> 13:28.007
They carry on the heritage of old music
while working on new creative endeavors,

13:29.017 --> 13:31.004
but they've been stuck in a rut lately.

13:31.004 --> 13:34.008
I'm sure interacting with you guys
will give them a nice stimulation.

13:34.008 --> 13:38.034
A cultural exchange? I like that idea!
We couldn't ask for anything better.

13:38.084 --> 13:42.097
Also, that scientific presentation
was quite interesting as well.

13:43.097 --> 13:47.072
There are those under me with
a rather odd interest in research.

13:47.072 --> 13:51.077
I was thinking we could send them here,
but would you mind that?

13:51.077 --> 13:54.023
Hmm... I wouldn't mind that.

13:54.073 --> 13:57.057
I'll pay you with something, of course.

13:57.057 --> 14:00.049
How about I offer a skill to you?

14:00.049 --> 14:01.078
A skill?

14:01.078 --> 14:02.086
That's right.

14:02.086 --> 14:07.016
I'll give you
"the secret skills of faith and favor."

14:07.016 --> 14:09.024
What's that? Sounds really cool!

14:09.024 --> 14:11.008
What are those?

14:11.008 --> 14:13.025
Oh, it's simple.

14:13.025 --> 14:19.025
It allows those faithful to you
to harness some of your powers.

14:21.013 --> 14:26.097
So you'll teach me this in exchange for
letting your researchers come stay here?

14:26.097 --> 14:28.018
Indeed.

14:28.018 --> 14:31.023
In a way,
this is my token of thanks to you.

14:31.069 --> 14:32.098
All right.

14:32.098 --> 14:34.098
I'll take your offer.

14:35.094 --> 14:37.048
Then we have a deal.

14:38.086 --> 14:40.044
Report.

14:40.044 --> 14:43.086
Secret skills of faith
and favor understood.

14:43.086 --> 14:45.049
Whoa!

14:45.049 --> 14:49.083
With this, maybe some of those under me
could gain access to Holy magic.

14:49.083 --> 14:51.037
By the way, Rimuru.

14:52.079 --> 14:58.021
There were some rather disagreeable
people among the dignitaries you invited.

14:58.021 --> 15:00.025
Were you aware of them?

15:00.077 --> 15:02.017
Yeah.

15:02.017 --> 15:03.055
Two of them, I believe.

15:03.055 --> 15:08.022
Mm. If you don't shirk your duty and keep
your wits about you, then very well.

15:08.022 --> 15:12.068
I do hope you will make efforts not to
denigrate the good name of the Octagram.

15:13.035 --> 15:14.019
Yeah.

15:15.044 --> 15:18.094
I tell you, that was a seriously
incredible performance!

15:18.094 --> 15:20.086
You should've checked it out, too, Hinata.

15:20.086 --> 15:24.086
Oh, shut up. I achieved what I set
out to do today. What's the problem?

15:25.036 --> 15:28.074
That yakisoba was surprisingly good, too.

15:28.074 --> 15:30.058
But really, why "Gimei"?

15:30.058 --> 15:32.062
Is that supposed to be
the word for "alias"?

15:33.062 --> 15:36.062
GIMEI'S TEPPANYAKI

15:38.004 --> 15:42.063
Actually, I'm more interested
in that research into magicules.

15:42.063 --> 15:46.034
You know, healing potions
don't really work on me.

15:46.034 --> 15:48.076
That's because my body
breaks down the magicules.

15:49.003 --> 15:53.014
And actually, there are some healing magics
that work on me and some that don't.

15:53.014 --> 15:57.009
Yeah, like, I'm affected
by magicules, too.

15:58.044 --> 16:02.061
When you jump between worlds,
it must've affected you in some way

16:02.061 --> 16:04.009
You haven't grown at all, for one.

16:04.009 --> 16:07.091
Whoa, can you please
don't put it that way?

16:07.091 --> 16:11.007
Like yeah, I haven't grown at all,
that's true and all.

16:11.007 --> 16:16.016
But still, Rimuru, what a fascinating
direction you gave to your researchers.

16:16.016 --> 16:20.071
No, they decided on the theme themselves.

16:20.071 --> 16:22.088
I only learned about it today.

16:22.088 --> 16:23.072
Huh?

16:23.072 --> 16:27.063
And you let them announce it to VIPs from around
the world without even knowing what it was?

16:27.063 --> 16:29.008
But look, what could I do?

16:29.008 --> 16:32.064
I want them to be independent!

16:34.064 --> 16:36.068
Okay, I did regret that a bit.

16:36.068 --> 16:40.036
I was really busy, but I should've
at least heard what it was first, right?

16:41.015 --> 16:43.044
You sure are something, Rimuru,
you know that?

16:43.044 --> 16:45.036
Yeah, honestly.

16:45.036 --> 16:48.065
Sometimes I seriously think
you're a real big shot, you know?

16:51.007 --> 16:53.028
We don't have money?!

16:53.028 --> 16:54.062
Yes.

16:54.062 --> 16:58.079
The tradesmen were all
hounding for payment in cash.

16:58.079 --> 17:01.004
No, that can't be, right?

17:01.004 --> 17:04.059
Don't we have all those assets
we got from Clayman's mansion?

17:05.003 --> 17:10.047
What about the 1,500 stellars
I got as restitution from Falmuth?

17:10.047 --> 17:11.037
Yeah.

17:11.037 --> 17:14.097
If we dipped into that, we could hold
a hundred more festivals and still have money!

17:15.043 --> 17:18.001
It's not the issue of funds.

17:18.001 --> 17:23.023
First, we can't convert
Clayman's assets into money.

17:23.023 --> 17:28.044
Those aren't the world's common currency
minted by the Dwarven kingdom.

17:28.044 --> 17:31.078
Also, stellar gold coins
hold too much value,

17:31.078 --> 17:34.024
we can't use them for
personal trades.

17:34.024 --> 17:38.025
That means although we have the money,
we don't have usable gold coins.

17:38.025 --> 17:39.075
That's right.

17:39.075 --> 17:43.004
It was already too late
by the time I noticed.

17:43.004 --> 17:45.075
All the gold coins I have already gone.

17:45.075 --> 17:48.026
Tempest is a new nation.

17:48.026 --> 17:51.013
Although we have economic power,
we have no credit to back it up.

17:51.013 --> 17:54.001
We can't enact IOUs
to pay for it later, either.

17:54.001 --> 17:59.018
I'm sure the big store owners I'm friends
with will be willing to agree to that.

17:59.018 --> 18:04.002
But the tradesman blanked at the idea
and demanded payment by common coins.

18:04.002 --> 18:07.061
It's those unfamiliar tradesmen
you talked about before, right?

18:07.061 --> 18:09.004
Indeed, sir.

18:09.004 --> 18:14.007
I see. Something tells me this
is being engineered by someone.

18:14.007 --> 18:19.041
I never expected someone
to meddle with us like this...

18:19.041 --> 18:23.062
So someone's trying
to ruin our reputation, then?

18:23.062 --> 18:25.025
I would imagine so.

18:25.025 --> 18:29.042
The international rules set by
the Council of the West stipulate that

18:29.042 --> 18:33.063
payments must be made with gold coins
minted in the Dwarven Kingdom.

18:33.063 --> 18:38.031
The claim the tradesmen are making are
valid under the Western Nations' laws.

18:38.031 --> 18:42.081
So they won't back off easily
if we force our rules on them?

18:42.081 --> 18:44.031
No, that won't work.

18:44.031 --> 18:46.099
Besides that, the tradesmen
could be conspiring together

18:46.099 --> 18:50.057
and intentionally causing a problem.

18:50.057 --> 18:53.032
Did someone from the Council do this?

18:53.086 --> 18:57.007
You'd need to resign yourself to endure
some losses to pull something like this.

18:57.007 --> 19:03.046
I find it hard to imagine their goal is
simply to ruin our nation's reputation.

19:03.046 --> 19:07.000
So we can't force
our own rules on them?

19:07.088 --> 19:08.096
Yeah.

19:08.096 --> 19:10.084
If we do force our rules on them,

19:10.084 --> 19:14.043
there's a chance the Western
Nations won't count us as allies.

19:15.004 --> 19:22.022
Since we want to play nice with humans,
we have to avoid that at all costs.

19:22.066 --> 19:28.019
But wasn't it your plan to join hands
with Thalion, Blumund, Dwargon,

19:28.019 --> 19:31.007
Falmuth... er, Falmenace,

19:31.007 --> 19:33.086
and Demon Lord Milim's domain,

19:33.086 --> 19:37.028
to create a co-prosperity sphere?

19:37.028 --> 19:39.074
With Tempest standing
as the center of it all,

19:40.024 --> 19:43.062
wouldn't it be a bigger loss to them
to ignore our presence?

19:46.026 --> 19:49.000
You truly are worthy of being
head secretary, Lady Shion.

19:49.000 --> 19:50.084
You are correct.

19:50.084 --> 19:51.088
"Aren't I?

19:51.088 --> 19:55.008
So why would they try to meddle with us?

19:55.008 --> 20:00.097
If they can't ignore us, wouldn't it
be better to try building trust with us?

20:01.091 --> 20:05.035
I'm shocked! Are you really Shion?

20:05.035 --> 20:05.098
Excuse me?

20:05.098 --> 20:09.069
People are truly strange creatures.

20:09.069 --> 20:11.098
They all must work together to survive,

20:11.098 --> 20:15.015
and yet they can't resist creating
a hierarchy among themselves.

20:15.015 --> 20:18.002
And if two groups of them
live next to each other,

20:18.002 --> 20:21.045
they continually squabble until
one proves itself superior to the other.

20:21.045 --> 20:27.005
The weak and pitiful fear nothing more
than losing their own vital interests.

20:27.005 --> 20:30.000
And in this case...

20:31.038 --> 20:33.042
Are you saying that the Council's worried

20:33.042 --> 20:36.088
the co-prosperity sphere
Great Rimuru makes puts them in jeopardy?

20:36.088 --> 20:38.091
Exactly.

20:39.093 --> 20:44.001
We should just crush these foolish rulers
who are incapable of understanding

20:44.001 --> 20:47.089
their position and refused
to accept Great Rimuru's kindness.

20:49.094 --> 20:51.098
So you agree, vice secretary?

20:51.098 --> 20:53.065
No, definitely no.

20:53.073 --> 20:54.009
Yes, sir.

20:54.009 --> 20:56.074
Yeah, she's still Shion, all right.

20:57.019 --> 20:59.049
Either way,
we can't let this go unaddressed.

20:59.049 --> 21:02.074
So Mjöllmile, when is payment due?

21:02.074 --> 21:04.024
You think we can manage?

21:04.024 --> 21:08.016
Yes, they're all enjoying
the festival as well,

21:08.016 --> 21:11.005
so they are willing to wait
until the day after it closes.

21:12.017 --> 21:14.042
So we only have two days left?

21:14.042 --> 21:17.063
Then, even if it means taking a loss,

21:17.063 --> 21:20.001
can we pay them with our gold bars?

21:20.001 --> 21:24.089
I imagine intelligent merchants
would take that offer,

21:25.043 --> 21:28.006
but I have to say no to that!

21:28.006 --> 21:29.064
Huh? Why?

21:29.064 --> 21:32.027
It's because then they'll look down on us!

21:32.027 --> 21:33.097
After that,

21:33.097 --> 21:39.015
they'll see us as a nation that will agree
to impossible deals, even at a loss!

21:39.063 --> 21:44.016
Show weakness to a merchant,
and they'd fleece you dry, huh.

21:44.016 --> 21:45.099
Yes, indeed.

21:45.099 --> 21:48.045
Well, no point worrying
too much about this.

21:49.058 --> 21:54.054
This is our nation, and if worse comes to worst,
we'll make them follow our rules!

21:54.054 --> 21:58.013
Don't overthink it
and just do what you can.

21:58.013 --> 21:59.067
Understood.

21:59.067 --> 22:02.001
Right. Meeting adjourned!

22:02.001 --> 22:03.018
Good work, everyone!

22:04.034 --> 22:06.068
How about we head out now, Mjöllmile?

22:06.068 --> 22:07.097
And you guys, too.

22:09.047 --> 22:10.085
H-Head out? Where to?

22:10.085 --> 22:14.031
To the town, of course!
We're in the middle of a festival, remember?

22:14.031 --> 22:17.009
Look at Benimaru.
He's all geared up to have some fun.

22:17.009 --> 22:20.053
But I need to start raising money...

22:20.053 --> 22:23.034
Oh, no point worrying about that for now!

22:23.034 --> 22:24.082
If it's not there, it's not there.

22:24.082 --> 22:28.006
Having you worked up so much that it
knocks you out is a bigger problem for us.

22:28.006 --> 22:31.058
I could never say no to you.

22:31.058 --> 22:34.054
I, Mjöllmile, am ready to take your offer!

22:38.042 --> 22:41.055
Don't overdo it, okay, Great Rimuru?

22:42.034 --> 22:44.097
And you, too, my brother.

22:44.097 --> 22:46.055
Yes, ma'am.

22:47.072 --> 22:51.007
THE FOUNDER'S FESTIVAL DAY 2
And so, with a light hangover,

22:51.007 --> 22:52.093
we got to Day 2 of
the Founder's Festival.

22:56.006 --> 23:01.078
We will now begin the main matches of
the Tempest Battle Tournament!

24:35.095 --> 24:38.083
Next time,
"The Battle Tournament."
